# Byte-compiled / cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# All generated artifacts live under data/. The resume-critical files are tracked
# (see the "NOT ignored" note below); everything heavy/regenerable is ignored.

# Transient gating-candidate checkpoints (training/manager.py writes these under
# data/Networks mid-episode - _candidate_tmp.keras / _gating_candidate.keras - and
# always deletes them afterward, but ignore them in case a run gets killed mid-gating).
data/Networks/_candidate_tmp.keras
data/Networks/_gating_candidate.keras

# Large raw-MCTS example pool. Regenerable via `python pretrain.py`, so not tracked.
data/PretrainExamples/

# Large, regenerable self-play artifacts from past runs. These sit at the repo root,
# outside data/, and nothing in the active code reads them (see CLAUDE.md/
# ARCHITECTURE_OVERVIEW.md); individual files run into the hundreds of MB - past
# GitHub's 100MB per-file limit - so they are never tracked.
self_play_Networks/
self_play_TrainingExamples/

# NOT ignored: data/Network.keras (current champion), data/Networks/ (promoted
# checkpoints), and data/TrainingExamples/ (replay buffer) are what project.py /
# pretrain.py resume from, so they need to travel to the Windows desktop for training
# to continue rather than restart.
